3026
03:37:57,380 --> 03:38:00,200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Speaker, and to the distinguished sponsor.

3027
03:38:03,760 --> 03:38:07,520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: After the Ateneo de Zamboanga school shooting,

3028
03:38:08,440 --> 03:38:17,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: DICT and CICC publicly raised the possibility of blocking Facebook as a last resort

3029
03:38:17,300 --> 03:38:23,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: over delayed takedowns of violent content, child safety concerns, and misinformation.

3030
03:38:24,100 --> 03:38:26,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Malakanyang later said there is no ban for now,

3031
03:38:27,380 --> 03:38:28,320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and that the government is cooperating.

3032
03:38:28,980 --> 03:38:30,740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And talks were held in Singapore.

3033
03:38:32,200 --> 03:38:35,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What really transpired in Singapore?

3034
03:38:35,760 --> 03:38:39,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Nagkaroon ko ba ng usapan po nung pumunta po kayo?

3035
03:38:39,840 --> 03:38:42,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Because I remember during committee hearing, Madam Chair,

3036
03:38:42,800 --> 03:38:47,440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: nabanggit na [unclear] Secretary, nagkaroon daw ng dialogue sa Singapore.

3037
03:38:47,820 --> 03:38:51,360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can you update us what transpired on that said meeting?

3038
03:38:51,460 --> 03:38:57,360
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes. Madam Secretary, if I'm not mistaken, members of the DICT and CICC,

3039
03:38:57,380 --> 03:39:04,960
Rep. Brian Poe: flew to Singapore to consult and explain the situation here in the Philippines to META.

3040
03:39:05,580 --> 03:39:13,700
Rep. Brian Poe: And I believe they're working towards an MOU, an MOA, rather, with META

3041
03:39:13,700 --> 03:39:19,300
Rep. Brian Poe: to be able to address the growing concerns of influence on minors here in the Philippines,

3042
03:39:19,600 --> 03:39:24,740
Rep. Brian Poe: among other concerns that are happening within the META platform, Madam Speaker.

3043
03:39:24,740 --> 03:39:26,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you.

3044
03:39:27,380 --> 03:39:31,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor,

3045
03:39:32,800 --> 03:39:41,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: one of the primary mandates of the DICT is the security of critical ICT infrastructure,

3046
03:39:41,540 --> 03:39:46,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: which includes the information assets of government, individuals, and businesses,

3047
03:39:47,460 --> 03:39:53,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: as well as the protection of consumers' privacy, security, and confidentiality.

3048
03:39:53,120 --> 03:39:57,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: My question will focus on DICT's follow-through,

3049
03:39:57,380 --> 03:39:58,620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: as well as the security of the META platform.

3050
03:39:58,620 --> 03:39:58,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The DICT also announced an agreement with META on online scams,

3051
03:39:58,980 --> 03:40:05,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: particularly those occurring through Facebook and other META platforms.

3052
03:40:05,820 --> 03:40:11,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The DICT announced an agreement with META as early as February 2026,

3053
03:40:12,900 --> 03:40:20,620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: covering fake investment schemes, phishing, digital fraud, online scams, and deep fakes.

3054
03:40:21,680 --> 03:40:24,740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What does the agreement actually entail, Mr. Speaker?

3055
03:40:27,380 --> 03:40:36,680
Rep. Brian Poe: So, Madam Speaker, the agreement that was being referred to is separate from the MOA that they're currently working on.

3056
03:40:37,020 --> 03:40:40,600
Rep. Brian Poe: And to update my colleague, because of the urgency,

3057
03:40:41,140 --> 03:40:47,900
Rep. Brian Poe: as of yesterday, the DICT and CICC have already started their technical working group with META

3058
03:40:47,900 --> 03:40:53,680
Rep. Brian Poe: to be able to address the concerns of our constituents with regards to these matters.

3059
03:40:53,680 --> 03:40:56,620
Rep. Brian Poe: However, on the status of the TWG,

3060
03:40:57,380 --> 03:40:58,820
Rep. Brian Poe: because they're just about to start,

3061
03:40:59,280 --> 03:41:03,480
Rep. Brian Poe: they're only doing role assignments and immediate target setting.

3062
03:41:04,800 --> 03:41:11,720
Rep. Brian Poe: But as the days go on, we'll see immediate action from the relevant agencies, Madam Speaker.

3063
03:41:12,600 --> 03:41:13,780
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

3064
03:41:14,040 --> 03:41:18,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: By the way, how many, as far as Facebook account,

3065
03:41:19,260 --> 03:41:24,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: do they have Facebook or the META as an office here in the Philippines?

3066
03:41:27,380 --> 03:41:35,820
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, I would like to confirm that Facebook does have a physical office here in the Philippines.

3067
03:41:36,160 --> 03:41:39,540
Rep. Brian Poe: However, we don't have jurisdiction over them, Madam Speaker,

3068
03:41:39,540 --> 03:41:41,380
Rep. Brian Poe: dahil marketing office lang po ito.

3069
03:41:41,580 --> 03:41:46,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, in short, Madam Speaker, wala talaga silang office, only marketing arm.

3070
03:41:47,000 --> 03:41:51,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ibig sabihin, pang-marketing, pang-recruit lang.

3071
03:41:51,480 --> 03:41:56,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, what I'm trying to say, do they have a country manager here in the Philippines?

3072
03:41:57,240 --> 03:41:59,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And how many employees do they employ?

3073
03:42:02,120 --> 03:42:05,680
Rep. Brian Poe: There's only a handful of employees here in the Philippines, Madam Speaker,

3074
03:42:05,780 --> 03:42:08,780
Rep. Brian Poe: and they don't have an official country manager for the Philippines.

3075
03:42:09,320 --> 03:42:13,600
Rep. Brian Poe: But I would like to assure my colleague that one of the terms that,

3076
03:42:13,740 --> 03:42:18,440
Rep. Brian Poe: the two of the terms that are being considered in this technical working group

3077
03:42:18,440 --> 03:42:23,440
Rep. Brian Poe: is one, that they do have a physical office here in the Philippines,

3078
03:42:24,040 --> 03:42:25,660
Rep. Brian Poe: a corporate office here in the Philippines,

3079
03:42:25,660 --> 03:42:26,940
Rep. Brian Poe: and that two,

3080
03:42:27,240 --> 03:42:34,820
Rep. Brian Poe: that they require the national ID already for users of META here in the Philippines.

3081
03:42:35,260 --> 03:42:36,320
Rep. Brian Poe: And it's been done before.

3082
03:42:36,480 --> 03:42:41,480
Rep. Brian Poe: I want to point that out, that Brazil has already implemented such a system

3083
03:42:41,480 --> 03:42:42,980
Rep. Brian Poe: because of their age restrictions.

3084
03:42:44,160 --> 03:42:44,840
Rep. Brian Poe: So, it is possible.

3085
03:42:44,840 --> 03:42:48,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker, what I'm trying to say, do they have office?

3086
03:42:49,160 --> 03:42:50,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Do they have managers?

3087
03:42:51,160 --> 03:42:52,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Not the marketing itself.

3088
03:42:53,180 --> 03:42:54,340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yun ang gusto naming mangyari.

3089
03:42:54,520 --> 03:42:54,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: See?

3090
03:42:54,660 --> 03:42:55,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: There's none.

3091
03:42:55,700 --> 03:42:56,980
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, we don't have jurisdiction.

3092
03:42:57,240 --> 03:42:58,300
Rep. Brian Poe: I agree with my colleague.

3093
03:42:58,540 --> 03:42:59,300
Rep. Brian Poe: It's ridiculous.

3094
03:42:59,720 --> 03:43:03,520
Rep. Brian Poe: Considering that the Philippines is the fifth largest population on META,

3095
03:43:03,960 --> 03:43:09,900
Rep. Brian Poe: that META does not have an actual country manager and a real office here in the Philippines,

3096
03:43:10,060 --> 03:43:17,440
Rep. Brian Poe: considering the amount of capital that this country provides META through its engagement on the platform.

3097
03:43:17,720 --> 03:43:19,760
Rep. Brian Poe: So, I agree with my colleague here.

3098
03:43:20,020 --> 03:43:21,820
Rep. Brian Poe: This is a priority for us.

3099
03:43:21,820 --> 03:43:26,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker, the distinguished sponsor mentioned a while ago that we are,

3100
03:43:26,880 --> 03:43:30,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: the fifth largest users of META.

3101
03:43:30,980 --> 03:43:35,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Imagine, the entire, sa buong mundo, pang lima tayo,

3102
03:43:36,140 --> 03:43:42,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and we're only, what, 120 million Filipinos compared to other countries,

3103
03:43:42,740 --> 03:43:43,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: transing billions.

3104
03:43:44,200 --> 03:43:46,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But again, so we're being ignored.

3105
03:43:46,860 --> 03:43:50,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I'm not trying to blame the ICT, Madam Speaker.

3106
03:43:50,880 --> 03:43:52,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ito po yung sinasabi natin.

3107
03:43:53,580 --> 03:43:56,600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: We keep on making their businesses.

3108
03:43:56,880 --> 03:43:57,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Big.

3109
03:43:57,680 --> 03:44:01,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But in return, hindi mo lang tayo mapansin.

3110
03:44:01,600 --> 03:44:06,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Not even as office here in the Philippines, hindi maibigay sa atin.

3111
03:44:07,140 --> 03:44:11,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And they have to follow the Philippine laws, Madam Speaker.

3112
03:44:12,280 --> 03:44:17,620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, my next question, ano po ang ginawa ng DICT?

3113
03:44:17,620 --> 03:44:22,620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Did you persuade them na magtayo kayo sa opisina?

3114
03:44:23,320 --> 03:44:25,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Opisina, that you have a country manager,

3115
03:44:25,920 --> 03:44:32,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: that you have the organizational structure that will look into sa mga scammers?

3116
03:44:32,800 --> 03:44:36,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ang dami nang lumalabas, kawawa ang ating mga kababayan.

3117
03:44:36,360 --> 03:44:39,040
Rep. Brian Poe: Well, the two non-negotiables, Madam Speaker,

3118
03:44:39,240 --> 03:44:42,620
Rep. Brian Poe: are one, that they open an actual office here in the Philippines

3119
03:44:42,620 --> 03:44:44,440
Rep. Brian Poe: so that they can be held accountable.

3120
03:44:44,880 --> 03:44:50,360
Rep. Brian Poe: And two, Madam Speaker, again, for the sake of accountability and protection on social media,

3121
03:44:50,360 --> 03:44:55,900
Rep. Brian Poe: the requirement of national ID in order to create or maintain your account on the META platform,

3122
03:44:55,920 --> 03:44:57,160
Rep. Brian Poe: here in the Philippines.

3123
03:44:57,300 --> 03:44:59,440
Rep. Brian Poe: So, these are steps that are being taken.

3124
03:45:00,000 --> 03:45:10,820
Rep. Brian Poe: To be fair to META, META seems open to these requirements and have even cited other countries in which they had similar requirements and acted on it.

3125
03:45:10,820 --> 03:45:21,440
Rep. Brian Poe: So we're moving in that direction and the results of this technical working group that just started, hopefully we'll be able to see it within the next few months.

3126
03:45:21,440 --> 03:45:39,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, the concern is that DICT has several programs, publicized partnerships and coordination mechanisms, but we know, but we don't have visibility of the result of those initiatives.

3127
03:45:40,400 --> 03:45:51,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What system does DICT currently have to ensure that actions announced by the department are actually monitored through implementation?

3128
03:45:51,440 --> 03:46:03,960
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, I want to share with my colleague here and all the members of Congress that there is actual action that DICT is taking to hold META accountable.

3129
03:46:03,960 --> 03:46:20,380
Rep. Brian Poe: And what I have here in my hand, Madam Speaker, is a copy of several documents that have been submitted to the Office of the Solicitor General to possibly build up a case against META for abuses that take place on their platform,

3130
03:46:20,380 --> 03:46:21,380
Rep. Brian Poe: which they turn...

3131
03:46:21,440 --> 03:46:22,620
Rep. Brian Poe: A blind eye too.

3132
03:46:23,260 --> 03:46:31,020
Rep. Brian Poe: So in this, we have in Annex A, a draft of a civil complaint, which was prepared by the DICT.

3133
03:46:31,020 --> 03:46:48,020
Rep. Brian Poe: In Annex B, there is a formal request drawing from global litigation precedents in Brazil, New Mexico, and Los Angeles that recognize platforms as active participants rather than passive intermediaries of actions taken on their platform.

3134
03:46:48,720 --> 03:46:51,020
Rep. Brian Poe: Annex C actually has...

3135
03:46:51,440 --> 03:47:01,600
Rep. Brian Poe: All the evidence and documentation of abuse, that's OSAEC, CSAEM, financial fraud, online debt harassment, illegal gambling,

3136
03:47:01,840 --> 03:47:09,240
Rep. Brian Poe: records of platform knowledge and inaction is also included in this document in Annex C.

3137
03:47:09,240 --> 03:47:17,540
Rep. Brian Poe: In Annex D, the National Privacy Commission asserted its regulatory jurisdiction over META

3138
03:47:17,540 --> 03:47:24,840
Rep. Brian Poe: in relation to the processing of personal data for AI-generated content and functionalities.

3139
03:47:25,160 --> 03:47:36,720
Rep. Brian Poe: And the NTC submitted its legal position paper on a test case for courts to propose action to be taken against Facebook in Annex E.

3140
03:47:36,720 --> 03:47:44,280
Rep. Brian Poe: So the DICT and its attached agencies aren't just sitting around waiting for something to happen.

3141
03:47:44,640 --> 03:47:47,520
Rep. Brian Poe: They've already prepared the necessary evidence, documents,

3142
03:47:47,540 --> 03:47:54,000
Rep. Brian Poe: and potential cases to hold META accountable should they not work together with our government.

3143
03:47:54,380 --> 03:47:59,500
Rep. Brian Poe: So I would like to request the assistance of a page to pass a copy of this to my colleague

3144
03:47:59,500 --> 03:48:04,100
Rep. Brian Poe: so that my colleague would be able to go over the document.

3145
03:48:04,780 --> 03:48:12,420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker, what if I file a House resolution in aid of legislation and I will summon the DICT

3146
03:48:12,420 --> 03:48:15,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and who will be the representatives from META?

3147
03:48:15,800 --> 03:48:17,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sino bang papadala lang?

3148
03:48:17,540 --> 03:48:24,600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kali mag-file ako ng House resolution with regard to what happened to Zamboanga massacre.

3149
03:48:24,800 --> 03:48:27,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And of course, yung mga kanilang violation.

3150
03:48:27,680 --> 03:48:29,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sino ang pupunta rito from META?

3151
03:48:30,940 --> 03:48:32,140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Anyone from META?

3152
03:48:32,780 --> 03:48:34,740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Will be held responsible?

3153
03:48:34,740 --> 03:48:45,540
Rep. Brian Poe: From the DICT, they themselves wrote directly to Mark Zuckerberg to ask him to confront these issues which we are facing.

3154
03:48:46,300 --> 03:48:46,740
Rep. Brian Poe: Although...

3155
03:48:47,540 --> 03:48:48,780
Rep. Brian Poe: There was no response.

3156
03:48:49,000 --> 03:48:53,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker, I don't think the founder, Mark Zuckerberg, will come here.

3157
03:48:54,020 --> 03:48:56,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Para sa atin, ganito lang tayo sa kanya.

3158
03:48:56,300 --> 03:48:58,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: They make a lot of money through Facebook.

3159
03:48:59,320 --> 03:49:03,140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Alam naman nila na puri karamihan is...

3160
03:49:03,140 --> 03:49:04,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I'm not saying the whole thing, no?

3161
03:49:04,840 --> 03:49:06,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Because I don't have...

3162
03:49:06,300 --> 03:49:08,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Myself, I don't have Facebook account, no?

3163
03:49:08,980 --> 03:49:14,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi alam ko maraming kalokohan dyan, pero maraming gumagamit at karamihan sa ating mga kababayan

3164
03:49:14,980 --> 03:49:17,380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ay kumikita naman dyan, in fairness.

3165
03:49:17,540 --> 03:49:18,820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: To Facebook, no?

3166
03:49:18,900 --> 03:49:19,440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: To META.

3167
03:49:19,820 --> 03:49:22,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But again, we're talking about responsibility.

3168
03:49:23,780 --> 03:49:28,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: We're talking about yung kailangan nila maging, ano sila rito, accountable.

3169
03:49:29,080 --> 03:49:33,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yan po ang kailangan natin, Madam Speaker.

3170
03:49:33,180 --> 03:49:39,440
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, though Mark Zuckerberg himself never showed up in countries like Brazil and others,

3171
03:49:39,800 --> 03:49:44,460
Rep. Brian Poe: they did send legal representation to confront the issues in other countries.

3172
03:49:44,620 --> 03:49:45,180
Rep. Brian Poe: So, I assume...

3173
03:49:46,000 --> 03:49:47,380
Rep. Brian Poe: Kung magkaroon po tayo ng isang...

3174
03:49:47,540 --> 03:49:50,160
Rep. Brian Poe: Kung magkaroon po tayo ng isang House Resolution investigating this,

3175
03:49:50,460 --> 03:49:56,980
Rep. Brian Poe: kailangan na kailangan magpadala ng representation ang META to confront these valid issues from the House of Representatives.

3176
03:49:57,780 --> 03:50:01,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor,

3177
03:50:02,620 --> 03:50:05,380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: the issue then is not the absence of initiatives,

3178
03:50:06,100 --> 03:50:14,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: but whether the ICT has sufficient mechanisms to monitor implementation and measure actual results.

3179
03:50:14,120 --> 03:50:17,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I appreciate the responses of the Department,

3180
03:50:17,540 --> 03:50:19,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and the good sponsor.

3181
03:50:20,080 --> 03:50:27,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: However, I remain concerned that there is still insufficient information before this body

3182
03:50:27,700 --> 03:50:34,440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: regarding the actual outcomes of the ICT's anti-scam initiatives.

3183
03:50:35,200 --> 03:50:39,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The Department has entered into agreement, established reporting mechanisms,

3184
03:50:40,800 --> 03:50:46,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and coordinated with private platforms and law enforcement agency.

3185
03:50:46,260 --> 03:50:47,380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But,

3186
03:50:47,540 --> 03:50:49,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: for purposes of budget review,

3187
03:50:50,600 --> 03:50:58,520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: this Committee must also be able to determine what happened after those actions were initiated.

3188
03:50:59,160 --> 03:51:00,360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Without that information,

3189
03:51:00,700 --> 03:51:09,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: it is difficult for Congress to properly assess whether the resources being requested are producing the intended outcomes.

3190
03:51:10,600 --> 03:51:11,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Accordingly, Madam Chair,

3191
03:51:11,960 --> 03:51:15,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: until those matters are a satisfactory address,

3192
03:51:16,700 --> 03:51:17,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and the Department can...

3193
03:51:17,540 --> 03:51:22,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and the Department can present measurables, deliverables.

3194
03:51:22,540 --> 03:51:28,480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker, it pains me, but I have no choice.

3195
03:51:29,520 --> 03:51:38,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I move that for consideration of the budget of the Department of Information and Communication Technology be deferred.

3196
03:51:40,800 --> 03:51:41,960
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: Madam Speaker,

3197
03:51:42,280 --> 03:51:43,080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader,

3198
03:51:43,080 --> 03:51:46,780
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: on the part of the majority,

3199
03:51:47,540 --> 03:51:55,680
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: we join the minority in the motion to defer the period of interpellations on the proposed budget

3200
03:51:55,680 --> 03:51:59,960
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: of the Department of Information and Communications Technology,

3201
03:52:00,520 --> 03:52:03,880
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: including its attached agencies.

3202
03:52:06,000 --> 03:52:10,200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Because of the wisdom of the minority,

3203
03:52:10,200 --> 03:52:16,200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: that the plan of the ICT insofar as curbing scams,

3204
03:52:17,540 --> 03:52:22,680
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and victimizing our children on the negative aspects,

3205
03:52:22,680 --> 03:52:24,200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: especially on their behavior,

3206
03:52:24,620 --> 03:52:26,260
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: has not been addressed well,

3207
03:52:26,920 --> 03:52:28,940
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: there is a motion from the minority,

3208
03:52:30,200 --> 03:52:32,260
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: duly supported by the majority,

3209
03:52:32,980 --> 03:52:40,120
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to defer consideration of the proposed budget of the Department of Information and Communications Technology,

3210
03:52:41,040 --> 03:52:42,660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: including its attached agencies.

3211
03:52:43,840 --> 03:52:44,940
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Do we hear an objection?

3212
03:52:46,460 --> 03:52:47,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Hearing none, said motion.

3213
03:52:47,540 --> 03:52:48,260
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Motion is approved.

3214
03:52:48,800 --> 03:52:51,160
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Consideration of the budget of DICT,

3215
03:52:51,640 --> 03:52:54,460
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the Department of Information and Communications Technology,

3216
03:52:55,200 --> 03:52:56,600
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: including its attached agencies,

3217
03:52:56,720 --> 03:52:57,500
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: hereby deferred.

3218
03:52:59,360 --> 03:53:00,660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session suspended.

3219
04:00:00,000 --> 04:00:03,840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: May we request the DOLE family to be seated so we can start?

3220
04:00:13,040 --> 04:00:14,300
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session resumed.

3221
04:00:15,540 --> 04:00:16,580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

3222
04:00:19,000 --> 04:00:26,020
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Speaker, I move to consider the proposed budget of the Department of Labor and Employment, including its attached agencies.

3223
04:00:27,280 --> 04:00:28,980
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: An objection? Hearing none.

3224
04:00:30,000 --> 04:00:39,280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The motion to consider the proposed budget of the Department of Labor and Employment, including its attached agencies, is hereby open.

3225
04:00:39,880 --> 04:00:40,840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

3226
04:00:41,380 --> 04:00:50,320
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Speaker, may we acknowledge the heads and officials of the Department of Labor and Employment, namely DOLE Secretary Francis Tolentino,

3227
04:00:50,320 --> 04:00:59,500
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco Kiko Benitez, Undersecretary Warren Miclat, Undersecretary Felipe Egargo Jr.,

3228
04:00:59,500 --> 04:01:10,740
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Undersecretary Carmela Torres, and we would also like to acknowledge the presence of the heads of attached agencies, regional directors, other officials and employees of DOLE.

3229
04:01:12,180 --> 04:01:26,000
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Department of Labor and Employment family, together with its attached agencies, headed by our very good friend, colleague, and former boss and mentor, Secretary Francis Tolentino,

3230
04:01:26,680 --> 04:01:29,340
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Ang gabay at tatay ng ating mga manggagawa.

3231
04:01:29,500 --> 04:01:34,280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: At kamanggagawa, maraming salamat po sa inyong pagdalo dito sa Kongreso.

3232
04:01:34,760 --> 04:01:35,540
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

3233
04:01:37,120 --> 04:01:45,420
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Vice Chair Rommel Angara of the Lone District of Aurora

3234
04:01:45,420 --> 04:01:53,700
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and the Honorable Vice Chair Maria Angela Garcia of the Third District of Bataan to sponsor the proposed budget of DOLE.

3235
04:01:54,600 --> 04:01:59,280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Vice Chair Rommel Angara is hereby recognized

3236
04:01:59,500 --> 04:02:02,080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Sponsor the budget of the Department of Labor and Employment.

3237
04:02:02,200 --> 04:02:09,920
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: And of course, the Honorable Vice Chair Maria Angela Garcia, sponsor of the proposed budget of TESDA, are hereby recognized.

3238
04:02:11,500 --> 04:02:12,320
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

3239
04:02:14,920 --> 04:02:16,580
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Maraming salamat po, Madam Speaker.

3240
04:02:18,420 --> 04:02:25,460
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ngayong gabing ito, at tayo na po ang huling magkakaroon ng depensa sa ating budget ng ating Department of Labor and Employment,

3241
04:02:25,900 --> 04:02:28,760
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kasama na po ang ating attached agencies, including TESDA.

3242
04:02:29,500 --> 04:02:38,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: For the NEP of 2027, Department of Labor and Employment has Php 47,057,355,000.

3243
04:02:38,000 --> 04:02:47,940
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sa aking mga kasamahan dito sa Kongreso, ang ating budget po noong ating 2026 GAA ay Php 61.2 billion.

3244
04:02:48,600 --> 04:02:59,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So mayroon po tayong Php 14.1 billion na nabawas sa ating pondo na alam kong napakahalaga pagdating sa pagdating sa pagservisyo ng mandato ng ating Departamento.

3245
04:02:59,500 --> 04:03:06,340
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At that same time, pagbibigay ng mga karagdagang skills to upskill our workforce in the future.

3246
04:03:07,000 --> 04:03:22,760
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ako ay naniniwala na sa ating mga kasamahan at pagdating ng ating mga susunod pa mga deliberasyon na sana ang hiling po natin ay madagdagan o may balikman lamang yung pondong kinakailangan para lubusang magampanan ng ating Departamento ang kanilang mandato.

3247
04:03:23,340 --> 04:03:28,280
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pangalawa, sa ating bagong Secretary Francis Tolentino, alam po ninyo,

3248
04:03:29,500 --> 04:03:43,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ang mga initiatives under his new leadership na kung saan sa aking palagay ay malaki ang maitutulong para sa ating Departamento at sa ating mga laborers and workers, hindi lamang sa NCR, bagkos sa buong Pilipinas.

3249
04:03:43,720 --> 04:03:52,580
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Una, ay hinihingi rin niya po sa Kongreso ang karagdagan na sana ay magkaroon ng karagdagang Php 75 million upang sa ating Labor Attorney's Office.

3250
04:03:52,580 --> 04:03:54,360
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ano po ito, aking mga kasamahan?

3251
04:03:54,820 --> 04:03:59,480
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Siyempre po, alam naman po natin na ang PAO ay libre na po sa ating mga manggagawa.

3252
04:03:59,500 --> 04:04:23,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Subalit, sa dami po ng kaso na mga kinakaharap ng ating PAO, minabuti ng ating butihing Secretary na mayroong tututok sa ating mga manggagawa, oras na ito ay magkaroon ng free legal assistance, yan po ang ating Labor Attorney's Office in conjunction o kasama po dito yung bagong itatayo na NALJ o National Academy for Labor Justice.

3253
04:04:23,960 --> 04:04:28,900
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kaya sa aking mga kasamahan, I'm sure ito po ay napakahalaga.

3254
04:04:29,500 --> 04:04:59,480
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: para ma-implement ngayong 2026 and moving forward hanggang 2027 para siguraduhin natin na ang ating mga workers, hindi lamang sa Metro Manila bagkos sa buong Pilipinas, ay magkaroon ng kahit papaano ay social protection at meron silang masasandalan pagdating ng oras ng kinakailangan. So Madam Speaker, this representation from the Lone District of Aurora is now ready for interpellation together with Maria Angela Garcia for TESDA. Madam Speaker, we're now open for interpellation.

3255
04:04:59,500 --> 04:05:00,800
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

3256
04:05:02,420 --> 04:05:10,980
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Elijah San Fernando of Partylist Kamanggagawa to interpolate on the proposed budget of the DOLE.

3257
04:05:11,380 --> 04:05:15,780
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Elijah San Fernando is hereby recognized for his interpolation.

3258
04:05:17,340 --> 04:05:26,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat po, Madam Speaker, at sa ating kaibigan, ang kagalang-galang na Romel Angara, sponsor po ng budget ng Department of Labor and Employment.

3259
04:05:27,620 --> 04:05:28,700
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Malinaw po.

3260
04:05:29,500 --> 04:05:32,820
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang mandato ng Department of Labor and Employment.

3261
04:05:33,340 --> 04:05:40,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ito ay ipagtanggol at itaguyod ang karapatan ng mga manggagawa.

3262
04:05:41,840 --> 04:05:53,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Diyan pa lamang po, Mr. Sponsor, Madam Speaker, napakabigat na na responsibilidad ang nakaatang sa Department of Labor and Employment.

3263
04:05:54,380 --> 04:05:57,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3264
04:05:57,980 --> 04:06:01,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang malaking tanong ng mga manggagawa,

3265
04:06:03,300 --> 04:06:08,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: bakit sa hinihinging budget ng Department of Labor and Employment,

3266
04:06:09,300 --> 04:06:16,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: 67% o tumataginting na 14 bilyong piso,

3267
04:06:17,840 --> 04:06:25,260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang ilalaan para sa DOLE, Office of the Secretary, particular sa programang tupad, Mr. Sponsor?

3268
04:06:27,980 --> 04:06:32,880
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: What is the question, Distinguished Colleague?

3269
04:06:33,180 --> 04:06:47,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Bakit po, 67% o tumataginting na 14 bilyong piso, ang ilalaan ng DOLE, Office of the Secretary, sa programang tupad, Mr. Sponsor?

3270
04:06:53,120 --> 04:06:56,680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you for that, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

3271
04:06:56,680 --> 04:06:57,420
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Alam mo po,

3272
04:06:57,980 --> 04:07:00,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pag dinisek mo po yung ating pondo ng Office of the Secretary,

3273
04:07:01,140 --> 04:07:03,480
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kasi pagdating po, doon lang po ilalagak yan.

3274
04:07:03,920 --> 04:07:08,780
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero eventually, pagdating ng implementation, it will be trickled down to the regional offices,

3275
04:07:09,240 --> 04:07:11,640
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: down to provincial levels, per district, per town,

3276
04:07:11,980 --> 04:07:16,560
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: para magkaroon po ng employment at tulong sa ating mga kababayan.

3277
04:07:16,820 --> 04:07:20,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Simple as that, Madam Speaker and ating Distinguished Colleague.

3278
04:07:20,000 --> 04:07:23,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, Mr. Sponsor, Madam Speaker,

3279
04:07:23,980 --> 04:07:27,620
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: binibigyang matwid ngayon ng Department of Labor and Employment,

3280
04:07:27,980 --> 04:07:34,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na mahigit kalahati ng budget na hinihingi ng DOLE for the Office of the Secretary,

3281
04:07:34,640 --> 04:07:40,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ay ilalaan sa tupad kung ang isa sa malaking mandato ng DOLE

3282
04:07:40,040 --> 04:07:44,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ay proteksyonan, ipagtanggol, at itaguyod ang karapatan ng mga manggagawa.

3283
04:07:45,340 --> 04:07:51,340
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Papaano maiintindihan ng mga manggagawa na ginagampanan ng DOLE

3284
04:07:51,340 --> 04:07:54,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang napakaraming mga responsibilidad na ito

3285
04:07:54,980 --> 04:07:57,700
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kung 67% ng budget,

3286
04:07:57,980 --> 04:08:01,320
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ay ilalagak natin sa Office of the Secretary,

3287
04:08:01,780 --> 04:08:03,560
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: partikular sa programang tupad.

3288
04:08:04,100 --> 04:08:06,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang binabanggit po ng butihing sponsor, Madam Speaker,

3289
04:08:07,360 --> 04:08:12,640
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ay para daw po makapag-provide ng mga emergency na trabaho.

3290
04:08:12,740 --> 04:08:13,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tama po ba ito, Mr. Sponsor?

3291
04:08:13,680 --> 04:08:17,180
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: That is correct, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

3292
04:08:17,180 --> 04:08:23,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, malinaw po ba na refleksyon ito ng labor policy ng ating pamahalaan

3293
04:08:23,180 --> 04:08:27,580
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kung saan mas binibigyang prioridad ang mga emergency jobs?

3294
04:08:27,980 --> 04:08:32,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sa halip ng lumikha ng mga trabahong pangmatagalan at dekalidad,

3295
04:08:32,200 --> 04:08:32,820
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Sponsor?

3296
04:08:34,060 --> 04:08:35,680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

3297
04:08:36,000 --> 04:08:39,820
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yes, alam mo, yung tupad was started during the pandemic.

3298
04:08:40,460 --> 04:08:41,240
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And I agree with you.

3299
04:08:41,800 --> 04:08:44,660
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero you also have to understand, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

3300
04:08:45,460 --> 04:08:48,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa ating bansa ng Pilipinas, unfortunately,

3301
04:08:48,480 --> 04:08:50,220
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: nagkaroon tayo ng mga natural disasters.

3302
04:08:51,040 --> 04:08:53,920
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Alam mo, pag nangyari ito, even the local governments,

3303
04:08:54,080 --> 04:08:55,400
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: I came from the local government,

3304
04:08:55,400 --> 04:08:56,820
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: minsan karamihan dyan,

3305
04:08:57,100 --> 04:08:57,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: walang pera,

3306
04:08:57,980 --> 04:09:03,580
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: para pang salba sa ating mga naaksidente, binagyo, so on and so forth.

3307
04:09:03,940 --> 04:09:07,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Even pag nagkaroon ng programa para sa ating transport group,

3308
04:09:07,300 --> 04:09:08,600
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: papasok po ang tupad.

3309
04:09:08,900 --> 04:09:14,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yes, I get your point na sinasabi po ninyo na dapat lamang ba ay trabaho natin.

3310
04:09:14,400 --> 04:09:16,640
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: You also have to understand o dapat po nating alalanin,

3311
04:09:17,580 --> 04:09:21,620
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: puwera sa polisiya na paggawa ng formats, programs ng DOLE,

3312
04:09:21,620 --> 04:09:27,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay kinakailangan na sa mandato rin ito ay magkaroon ng trabaho para sa ating mamamayang Pilipino.

3313
04:09:27,980 --> 04:09:34,200
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: It is not per se na kinakailangan natin na ito ay patuloy na ginagawa,

3314
04:09:34,380 --> 04:09:37,100
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pero unfortunately, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

3315
04:09:37,380 --> 04:09:39,540
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ito po ay at the end of the day,

3316
04:09:39,940 --> 04:09:42,360
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kada probinsya at ang buong bansa ay talaga minsan,

3317
04:09:42,660 --> 04:09:46,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: unfortunately, ay nangangailangan ng ayuda at tulong para sa ating mga mamamayan.

3318
04:09:47,700 --> 04:09:49,860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maganda po na nabanggit, Madam Speaker,

3319
04:09:50,800 --> 04:09:52,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng ating butihing sponsor,

3320
04:09:52,920 --> 04:09:57,320
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na meron tayong mga isinasaalang-alang na mga konsiderasyon gaya ng krisis.

3321
04:09:57,980 --> 04:10:00,760
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ngunit, Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3322
04:10:01,280 --> 04:10:06,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: hindi po tinatanggap ng representasyong ito na gagamitin dahilan ang krisis

3323
04:10:06,960 --> 04:10:09,700
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: para sa paglobo ng budget ng tupad.

3324
04:10:10,300 --> 04:10:13,140
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: In fact, Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3325
04:10:13,520 --> 04:10:14,500
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: makikita natin,

3326
04:10:15,940 --> 04:10:20,340
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: sa loob ng sampung taon mula 2016,

3327
04:10:21,760 --> 04:10:24,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: hindi nagbago, virtually the same,

3328
04:10:24,460 --> 04:10:26,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang pondong inilalaan

3329
04:10:27,980 --> 04:10:30,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng mga trabaho o mandato

3330
04:10:30,880 --> 04:10:33,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng Dole Office of the Secretary

3331
04:10:33,120 --> 04:10:34,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: samantalang kitang-kita

3332
04:10:34,840 --> 04:10:37,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang papalubo at papalaking bilang

3333
04:10:37,900 --> 04:10:40,060
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng inilalagak natin sa tupad.

3334
04:10:40,960 --> 04:10:42,380
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, hindi po maaaring sabihin

3335
04:10:42,380 --> 04:10:44,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na dahil sa krisis, Madam Speaker,

3336
04:10:45,660 --> 04:10:48,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: dahil bago pa man magkaroon ng krisis,

3337
04:10:48,640 --> 04:10:51,220
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang Dole, batay sa kanyang budget,

3338
04:10:51,700 --> 04:10:54,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: papalaki ng papalaki ang inilalagak sa tupad

3339
04:10:54,940 --> 04:10:56,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kaysa palakihin ang budget

3340
04:10:56,940 --> 04:10:57,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: doon sa iba pa.

3341
04:10:57,980 --> 04:11:00,320
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ano ang mga funksyon ng Department of Labor and Employment?

3342
04:11:00,400 --> 04:11:01,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Sponsor.

3343
04:11:01,720 --> 04:11:03,520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

3344
04:11:04,000 --> 04:11:05,180
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: I'd like to correct the facts.

3345
04:11:05,480 --> 04:11:09,180
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sa Office of the Secretary, it's not 67%, but 52%.

3346
04:11:09,180 --> 04:11:12,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: For the record, Distinguished Colleague,

3347
04:11:12,660 --> 04:11:13,120
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: and secondly,

3348
04:11:13,920 --> 04:11:15,720
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: tama po, but you also have to understand,

3349
04:11:16,180 --> 04:11:18,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: tupad per se is not just tupad per se.

3350
04:11:18,280 --> 04:11:21,580
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: It also includes the government internship program

3351
04:11:21,580 --> 04:11:23,780
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na kung saan yung ating mga fresh graduates

3352
04:11:23,780 --> 04:11:25,540
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay papasok sa ating mga gobyerno

3353
04:11:25,540 --> 04:11:27,820
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: upang sagayoy mag-gain sila ng employability

3354
04:11:27,820 --> 04:11:27,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: at mag-gain sila ng employability

3355
04:11:27,980 --> 04:11:29,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: alam naman po natin dito sa ating bansa

3356
04:11:29,980 --> 04:11:33,240
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na kung saan karamihan ng mga ating employers

3357
04:11:33,240 --> 04:11:35,880
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay nangangailangan ng kinakailangan experience

3358
04:11:35,880 --> 04:11:37,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: para ito ay sila'y ma-hire.

3359
04:11:37,680 --> 04:11:39,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And in fact, sabi ko nga,

3360
04:11:39,200 --> 04:11:40,800
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: because of this situation,

3361
04:11:41,260 --> 04:11:43,680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay ito po ay maraming mga fresh graduates

3362
04:11:43,680 --> 04:11:44,680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ang makikinabang dito.

3363
04:11:45,040 --> 04:11:46,360
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sabi ko nga, ang isa sa mandato

3364
04:11:46,360 --> 04:11:47,820
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ng ating departemento

3365
04:11:47,820 --> 04:11:49,540
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay mag-create ng ating mga trabaho

3366
04:11:49,540 --> 04:11:53,400
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: not only for the normal na manggagawa

3367
04:11:53,400 --> 04:11:56,060
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: but also sa ating mga fresh graduates

3368
04:11:56,060 --> 04:11:56,840
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: dito sa ating bansa.

3369
04:11:56,840 --> 04:11:57,840
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

3370
04:11:57,980 --> 04:12:00,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3371
04:12:00,360 --> 04:12:03,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: binabanggit po ng DOLE na hindi 67%,

3372
04:12:03,300 --> 04:12:04,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kundi 52% lamang.

3373
04:12:05,500 --> 04:12:07,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero malinaw po, doon sa budget ng DOLE,

3374
04:12:07,780 --> 04:12:09,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: wala naman kasing distinksyon

3375
04:12:09,200 --> 04:12:10,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang TUPAD at GIP.

3376
04:12:11,820 --> 04:12:13,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So kapag sinuma natin,

3377
04:12:13,160 --> 04:12:17,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: 67% ang nasa TUPAD, hindi 52%.

3378
04:12:17,100 --> 04:12:19,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Be that as it may, Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker,

3379
04:12:20,540 --> 04:12:23,240
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang punto natin, mahigit kalahati pa rin

3380
04:12:23,240 --> 04:12:25,620
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng pondo ang inilalagak sa TUPAD.

3381
04:12:25,620 --> 04:12:26,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kaya ako po ito tinanong,

3382
04:12:26,980 --> 04:12:28,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3383
04:12:28,980 --> 04:12:32,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kasi sa 2025 COA findings,

3384
04:12:32,980 --> 04:12:37,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: sangkatutak na irregularidad ang nakita sa TUPAD.

3385
04:12:37,980 --> 04:12:40,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Halimbawa, Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3386
04:12:40,980 --> 04:12:42,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: base sa audit findings ng COA,

3387
04:12:42,980 --> 04:12:45,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: may mga benepisaryo ang TUPAD

3388
04:12:45,980 --> 04:12:48,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na nakakatanggap ng payout,

3389
04:12:48,980 --> 04:12:50,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: hindi lang po isang beses,

3390
04:12:50,980 --> 04:12:52,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: hindi lang dalawang beses,

3391
04:12:52,980 --> 04:12:56,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kundi tatlo hanggang apat na beses,

3392
04:12:56,980 --> 04:12:59,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na nakakatanggap ng payout.

3393
04:12:59,980 --> 04:13:05,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mismong DOLE ay nagva-violate ng guidelines o rule

3394
04:13:05,980 --> 04:13:07,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: pagdating sa TUPAD.

3395
04:13:07,980 --> 04:13:10,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: One per family per year.

3396
04:13:10,980 --> 04:13:14,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tapos ngayon, nagre-request uli ang Department of Labor and Employment,

3397
04:13:14,980 --> 04:13:16,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3398
04:13:16,980 --> 04:13:20,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng pagkalaki-laking budget na naman sa TUPAD

3399
04:13:20,980 --> 04:13:25,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na hindi pa nare-resolve ba ang sistema dito

3400
04:13:25,980 --> 04:13:28,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: sa mga benepisaryo ng TUPAD.

3401
04:13:28,980 --> 04:13:30,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Sponsor.

3402
04:13:30,980 --> 04:13:33,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

3403
04:13:33,980 --> 04:13:38,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yes, to answer directly sa ating katanungan ng ating sponsor,

3404
04:13:38,980 --> 04:13:41,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: I clarify that also to the Department.

3405
04:13:41,980 --> 04:13:44,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Siguro ang tinutukoy niyo po dito ay yung 1,275

3406
04:13:44,980 --> 04:13:47,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na naka-finlag ng COA, na Commission on Audit,

3407
04:13:47,980 --> 04:13:51,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na kung saan nakatanggap ito di umano ng dalawang beses.

3408
04:13:51,980 --> 04:13:54,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: For the record, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

3409
04:13:54,980 --> 04:13:56,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pinanong na po natin kung sa regional director,

3410
04:13:56,980 --> 04:14:00,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kung saan region ito ay nangyari base doon sa ating COA report.

3411
04:14:00,980 --> 04:14:06,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At doon po sa sinasabing 1,275, may explanation po dyan at ito po iyon.

3412
04:14:06,980 --> 04:14:12,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Una, yung 1,275 na binabanggit ay nagkamali po yun sa database lamang.

3413
04:14:12,980 --> 04:14:17,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Because kasama po doon sa mga 1,275 na iyon,

3414
04:14:17,980 --> 04:14:23,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: let me reiterate, Mr. Distinguished Colleague, na yes, tama ka doon sa sinabi mong isang beses lamang.

3415
04:14:23,980 --> 04:14:27,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pwede magtupad. Pero there's an exception to it.

3416
04:14:27,980 --> 04:14:30,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pag may kalamidad, pwedeng umulit po. That's for the record.

3417
04:14:30,980 --> 04:14:37,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero nung ito ay nating nadiskubre doon sa database po, nagkamali lamang sa database.

3418
04:14:37,980 --> 04:14:40,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At ito ay naayos na po natin sa Commission on Audit.

3419
04:14:40,980 --> 04:14:49,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At kinalabasan po dito na 15 lamang out of the 1,275 ang nagkaroon ng doubling payment.

3420
04:14:49,980 --> 04:14:52,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And for the record, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

3421
04:14:52,980 --> 04:14:58,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: doon sa labing limang iyon, sinigurado rin po natin, siyempre, sabi ko nga po, ang dole ay laging susunod.

3422
04:15:00,000 --> 04:15:10,720
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa alituntunin ng batas at lalo na sa sarili niyang requirement na dapat isang beses lamang bayaran ang isang nagmembro o nagtrabaho para sa tupad.

3423
04:15:11,060 --> 04:15:21,100
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And for information of the body, kahit i-double check po natin, yung labing limang recipient po yun ay nakuha na po muli yung ating pondo

3424
04:15:21,100 --> 04:15:27,060
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: dahil nagkamali nga po at yan po ay ni-report na po namin sa COA, Madam Speaker at Distinguished Colleague.

3425
04:15:27,060 --> 04:15:38,060
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Sponsor, Madam Speaker, hindi lang po 1,275 beneficiaries. Batay po sa COA findings, meron din pong nakakuha sa Saksargen,

3426
04:15:38,700 --> 04:15:49,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: 330 persons collected assistance twice, 57 collected three times, and 132 collected four times.

3427
04:15:49,460 --> 04:15:56,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So hindi po po pwedeng gamitin na palusot ng dole na meron lang simpleng problema sa database.

3428
04:15:56,020 --> 04:16:02,660
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Mr. Sponsor, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, hindi po kami nagpapalusot, Distinguished Colleague.

3429
04:16:03,140 --> 04:16:09,080
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Based dun po sa mga binanggit po niyo sa Saksargen and the rest, all of those are already settled sa COA.

3430
04:16:09,220 --> 04:16:16,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sabi ko nga po, hindi po po pwedeng kami po ay very strict pertaining sa implementation ng hindi lamang sa tupad,

3431
04:16:16,320 --> 04:16:19,920
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: bagkos sa lahat ng programa ng ating Department of Labor and Employment.

3432
04:16:19,920 --> 04:16:26,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At sisiguraduin ko po sa inyo, after this, we can give you the data na kung saan na binigay na po namin sa Commission on Oil,

3433
04:16:26,020 --> 04:16:28,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: at nasettle na po yung lahat ng ating gagawin.

3434
04:16:28,340 --> 04:16:34,700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: In short, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, dun sa mga binanggit po natin, may ito be Saksargen, may ito be Zamboanga Peninsula,

3435
04:16:35,140 --> 04:16:42,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: at the end of the day, kahit saan po yan, sisiguraduin namin, sabi ko nga po, minsan nagkakamali at inaamin during the aking example,

3436
04:16:43,480 --> 04:16:52,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pero sinisigurado namin, nire-retract natin ito, ginagawa natin tama at sumusunod sa alituntunin ng ating Commission on Audit, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

3437
04:16:52,020 --> 04:16:55,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, maraming salamat po sa sponsor.

3438
04:16:56,020 --> 04:17:08,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, dahil pinagtibay lang ng ating butihing sponsor, ang ating binabanggit kanina, na ang pondo, malaking pondo na inilalagak sa Dole, Office of the Secretary, ay napupunta sa Tupad,

3439
04:17:09,040 --> 04:17:13,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at mas pinagtibay pa ito ng ating pinag-uusapan kanina. At dyan po ako tutungo.

3440
04:17:14,600 --> 04:17:19,240
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ulitin lang po natin, ano nga ba ang mandato ng Department of Labor and Employment?

3441
04:17:20,240 --> 04:17:25,920
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ipagtanggol at itaguyod ang karapatan ng mga manggagawa.

3442
04:17:26,020 --> 04:17:36,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At isa sa paraan para itaguyod at ipagtanggol ang karapatan ng mga manggagawa ay sa pamamagitan ng labor inspeksyon.

3443
04:17:37,860 --> 04:17:49,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kaya nga po, kinikilala mismo ni Sekretary ng butihing Sekretary ng Department of Labor and Employment, kulang naman talaga ang mga labor inspectors.

3444
04:17:49,680 --> 04:17:55,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kaya kailangan natin dagdagan ng budget. Ito po ang malaking tanong.

3445
04:17:56,020 --> 04:18:06,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor, kung kinikilala ng Department of Labor and Employment ang malaking kakulangan sa mga inspektor,

3446
04:18:07,020 --> 04:18:14,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: bakit sa halip nalagakan ng mas malaking pondo ang ating mga labor inspektor ay inilalaan ito muli sa Tupad?

3447
04:18:16,100 --> 04:18:20,640
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Papaano ngayon tinitindigan ng Department of Labor and Employment ang kanyang mandato?

3448
04:18:20,640 --> 04:18:26,000
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kung sa simpleng labor inspektor ay hindi nito magawang tindigan ang kanyang mandato.

3449
04:18:26,020 --> 04:18:33,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, maraming salamat po dun sa pagbigay mo ng impormasyon na iyon. Bakit?

3450
04:18:33,020 --> 04:18:41,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Una, kasi nga po, tandaan po natin, pag in terms of plantilya positions, it has to run through the Department of Budget and Management.

3451
04:18:41,020 --> 04:18:50,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At sinabi na rin po natin during the budget hearing, ang actual plantilya positions po natin, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, ay 1,210.

3452
04:18:50,020 --> 04:18:54,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero ang ating actual lamang is around 1,046.

3453
04:18:54,020 --> 04:18:55,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At nabanggit din po sa

3454
04:18:55,020 --> 04:18:56,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: nasabing

3455
04:18:56,020 --> 04:19:10,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: budget hearing, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, sa lawak ng kakailangan inspeksyonin, and again, I'd like to quote the Secretary, sa Region 3 alone, mahigit 7,000 na ang kailangang inspeksyunin.

3456
04:19:10,020 --> 04:19:19,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Iyon po ay isang region lamang po. Pero kapag buong kabuan, sa suma total ay halos kailangan mo ng 9,000 na labor inspectors.

3457
04:19:19,020 --> 04:19:25,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At iyan po ay binanggit po natin nung nanakaraang budget hearing ng Department of Labor and Employment na sana,

3458
04:19:25,020 --> 04:19:39,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: not in one year, kahit staggered po, kahit within 10 years, pero sana para lalo natin mapagsilbihan yung ating mga manggagawa, maportereksyonan sila doon sa mga ating labor inspections, ay sana ay madagdagan ito eventually in the long run.

3459
04:19:39,020 --> 04:19:43,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kaya nga po, Mr. Sponsor, hindi po nasagot ang tanong.

3460
04:19:43,020 --> 04:19:47,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Nangangailangan ng malaking bilang na mga labor inspector ang DOLE.

3461
04:19:47,020 --> 04:19:53,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero sa halip na ilagak ng Office of the Secretary ng DOLE ang pondo sa mga labor inspector,

3462
04:19:53,020 --> 04:19:59,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: mas minarapat ng DOLE na maglagak ng mas malaking pondo sa TUPAD.

3463
04:19:59,020 --> 04:20:03,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Hindi po sinasagot ng Department of Labor and Employment.

3464
04:20:03,020 --> 04:20:07,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: TUPAD? Labor Inspector.

3465
04:20:07,020 --> 04:20:11,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Just to prove a point, Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3466
04:20:11,020 --> 04:20:19,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: alam niyo po kung gaano ka-absurd yung itsura ng budget ng Department of Labor and Employment, Office of the Secretary?

3467
04:20:19,020 --> 04:20:21,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Admin cost ng TUPAD?

3468
04:20:21,020 --> 04:20:25,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: 712 million pesos.

3469
04:20:27,020 --> 04:20:35,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Samantala, ang sahod ng mga labor inspector, 605 million pesos lang.

3470
04:20:35,020 --> 04:20:39,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ano ba namang klaseng kalokohan yan, Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor?

3471
04:20:39,020 --> 04:20:47,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mas malaki ang nilalagak sa admin cost ng TUPAD kaysa pagpapasahod ng mga labor inspector.

3472
04:20:47,020 --> 04:20:49,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Batid po ba ng Department of Labor and Employment?

3473
04:20:49,020 --> 04:20:52,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Gaano kahirap ang buhay ng mga inspector?

3474
04:20:52,020 --> 04:20:56,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ako po mismo, ang kinatawang ito, ay sumama sa mga inspector sa Laguna.

3475
04:20:56,020 --> 04:21:03,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tapos ang maririnig po natin ngayon, eh mas okay na na mas lakihan ng budget sa TUPAD kaysa sa mga labor inspector.

3476
04:21:03,020 --> 04:21:09,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At ang gagamitin na dahilan, eh keso kulang ang budget o mahirap yung mga proseso.

3477
04:21:09,020 --> 04:21:15,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Hindi po maunawaan nito, Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor ng mga manggagawa.

3478
04:21:17,020 --> 04:21:18,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague,

3479
04:21:18,020 --> 04:21:21,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: unang-unang, I'd like to go back na sinabi mong hindi nasagot.

3480
04:21:21,020 --> 04:21:23,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sinagot ko po yung katanungan.

3481
04:21:23,020 --> 04:21:27,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kasi nga po, hindi naman nakalagak yan sa DOLE per se.

3482
04:21:27,020 --> 04:21:31,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kaya nga po hinihingi ng aming Departamento.

3483
04:21:31,020 --> 04:21:35,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Again, I'm sure you're familiar, alam mo po yung proseso, Congressman Eli,

3484
04:21:35,020 --> 04:21:40,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na hindi basta-basta ay pipwedeng ikaw ay maglagay lamang ng ating mga inspectors.

3485
04:21:40,020 --> 04:21:43,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: It has to go through the process, DBM, so on and so forth.

3486
04:21:43,020 --> 04:21:46,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And yun po ay sinagot po natin nung ulang statement po agad natin.

3487
04:21:46,020 --> 04:21:47,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ngayon, patukol naman ito, eh.

3488
04:21:47,020 --> 04:21:51,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ngayon, patukol naman doon sa ating mga pasweldo ng ating mga ano,

3489
04:21:51,020 --> 04:21:55,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: based doon sa records po namin,

3490
04:21:55,020 --> 04:21:58,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: yung 524 million na pasweldo natin,

3491
04:21:58,020 --> 04:21:59,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: P.S.

3492
04:21:59,020 --> 04:22:01,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: mas mataas po kesa doon sa ating

3493
04:22:01,020 --> 04:22:05,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: P.S. pa lang po ang binibilang natin dito, Mr. Sponsor.

3494
04:22:05,020 --> 04:22:08,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So kapag sinuma natin, mas malaki pa rin ang admin cost ng tupad

3495
04:22:08,020 --> 04:22:12,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kaysa sa pasweldo ng mga labor inspector.

3496
04:22:12,020 --> 04:22:14,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Sponsor?

3497
04:22:14,020 --> 04:22:16,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pasweldo? Ano pa yung admin?

3498
04:22:16,020 --> 04:22:19,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yes. It is the part of the...

3499
04:22:19,020 --> 04:22:22,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: parte po yun nung sa ating sweldo, Madam Speaker,

3500
04:22:22,020 --> 04:22:24,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kaya nga po, yun po ang binabigit po.

3501
04:22:24,020 --> 04:22:26,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kasi admin cost po kasi is 5%. Diba?

3502
04:22:26,020 --> 04:22:28,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tama po. Nasa special provision. Tama po.

3503
04:22:28,020 --> 04:22:29,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yes. That's correct.

3504
04:22:29,020 --> 04:22:33,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kaya ang pinupunto po ng kinatawang ito, eh bakit mas malaki ang hinihinging budget

3505
04:22:33,020 --> 04:22:37,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng DOLE Office of the Secretary sa tupad,

3506
04:22:37,020 --> 04:22:40,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: 5% of which mapupunta sa admin cost,

3507
04:22:40,020 --> 04:22:44,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: samantalang napakalaki ng problema at pangangailangan sa mga labor inspector.

3508
04:22:44,020 --> 04:22:45,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: This is what I'm pointing about.

3509
04:22:45,020 --> 04:22:47,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

3510
04:22:47,020 --> 04:22:51,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang daming dapat nai-inspect ng mga business establishments

3511
04:22:51,020 --> 04:22:54,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: pero mas pinipili ng Department of Labor and Employment

3512
04:22:54,020 --> 04:22:56,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na maglagak sa tupad.

3513
04:22:56,020 --> 04:23:00,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Eh paano matitiyak na napoproteksyonan ang karapatan ng mga manggagawa

3514
04:23:00,020 --> 04:23:04,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kung puro tupad ang Department of Labor and Employment?

3515
04:23:06,020 --> 04:23:08,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague,

3516
04:23:08,020 --> 04:23:10,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sabi ko nga po kanina,

3517
04:23:10,020 --> 04:23:12,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pertaining doon sa ating tupad,

3518
04:23:12,020 --> 04:23:14,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: it is not only per se na tupad.

3519
04:23:14,020 --> 04:23:18,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Binanggit niyo po yan sa ating Government Internship Program.

3520
04:23:18,020 --> 04:23:22,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero pag sino matutal mo po, hindi naman po kami nagkulang pertaining sa ating pinaglalaban.

3521
04:23:22,020 --> 04:23:24,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: I agree with you. Bakit?

3522
04:23:24,020 --> 04:23:28,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kaya nga po kami nagre-request ng karagdagan.

3523
04:23:28,020 --> 04:23:33,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: That was clear as day na sana kung kami ay tutulungan ng kapulungan na ito

3524
04:23:33,020 --> 04:23:35,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kasama ang Senado at ating national budget,

3525
04:23:35,020 --> 04:23:39,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kaya nga po ang kinakailangan na plantilya positions

3526
04:23:39,020 --> 04:23:42,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: based sa ating statement nung ating budget healing

3527
04:23:42,020 --> 04:23:46,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay 9,000 na labor inspectors ang kailangan.

3528
04:23:46,020 --> 04:23:49,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Alam mo, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague,

3529
04:23:49,020 --> 04:23:52,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: it is very very difficult to balance everything.

3530
04:23:52,020 --> 04:23:55,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Maraming pangangailangan pero ito ay kapos lamang.

3531
04:23:55,020 --> 04:23:58,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Maraming mandato ang ating Departamento.

3532
04:23:58,020 --> 04:24:00,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: One, magbigay ng trabaho.

3533
04:24:00,020 --> 04:24:06,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pangalawa, to secure the safetiness of our workers in every aspect possible.

3534
04:24:06,020 --> 04:24:10,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So sabi ko nga po, hindi naman tayo magkakaroon ng malaking problema

3535
04:24:10,020 --> 04:24:13,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kung ito ay sapat yung ating pondo.

3536
04:24:13,020 --> 04:24:16,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: But, kahit hindi po sapat yung pondo namin,

3537
04:24:16,020 --> 04:24:19,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ito po ay nagagampanan naman namin yung aming trabaho.

3538
04:24:19,020 --> 04:24:23,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yan ay based dun sa results ng ating mga performance sa NLRC,

3539
04:24:23,020 --> 04:24:26,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa ating mga patrabaho, sa job start.

3540
04:24:26,020 --> 04:24:32,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: In fact, nung September 14, nagkaroon po tayo ng nationwide na programa

3541
04:24:32,020 --> 04:24:34,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ang ating Department of Labor and Employment.

3542
04:24:34,020 --> 04:24:39,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So again, we are not just focused o di lang kami nagtutuon sa isang programa.

3543
04:24:39,020 --> 04:24:41,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

3544
04:24:41,020 --> 04:24:47,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Sponsor, Madam Speaker, hindi nga po nagtutugma yung binabanggit nyo

3545
04:24:47,020 --> 04:24:50,020
