Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: In fact, ang ating sekretary pa mismo ang nag-file sa ating mga korte na kung saan ang tindig o opisyal na tindig ng ating Departamento

3946
04:38:21,720 --> 04:38:30,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: together with the Office of the Solicitor General na dapat ito ay legal kasi walang jurisdiction ang korte

3947
04:38:30,260 --> 04:38:36,620
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: at dapat ito ay ipatupad ng ating mga korts at dapat sana ayaw makialam.

3948
04:38:36,620 --> 04:38:44,380
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So in fact, yung ating Wage Order 28 na 60 pesos, and ito po, importanteng-importante po ito, Madam Speaker. Bakit?

3949
04:38:45,480 --> 04:38:48,240
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yung Wage Order 28, 60 pesos.

3950
04:38:49,320 --> 04:38:51,240
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Doon sa Wage Order 27,

3951
04:38:51,720 --> 04:38:52,860
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: 85 pesos.

3952
04:38:53,260 --> 04:39:02,520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero, nakakalimutan banggitin doon lagi na sa Wage Order 27, sa taong 2026, ay it's also 60 pesos.

3953
04:39:02,520 --> 04:39:05,140
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Patunay lamang, patapusin mo ako, Distinguished Colleague,

3954
04:39:05,640 --> 04:39:13,920
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sapagkat sa pagkakataong yun, makikita natin na ang Departamento ay nagtatrabaho. Bakit?

3955
04:39:14,640 --> 04:39:20,320
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Simpleng-simple lang naman, kung kami walang malasakit o hindi ginagampanan ang aming tungkulin,

3956
04:39:20,760 --> 04:39:21,520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: [unclear] sana,

3957
04:39:21,720 --> 04:39:24,000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pinabayaan na lang namin yung Wage Order 27.

3958
04:39:24,400 --> 04:39:24,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Subalit hindi.

3959
04:39:25,620 --> 04:39:28,300
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sa mandato na binigay ng Kongreso at Senado at ang taong bayan,

3960
04:39:29,360 --> 04:39:34,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ang ating Wage Board, kumilos, nagpulong, nagpublic hearing,

3961
04:39:34,500 --> 04:39:42,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: para sa gayo yung magkaroon ng economic relief o katumbas ng ating 60 pesos na dapat dagdag sa Wage Order number 27.

3962
04:39:42,960 --> 04:39:47,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So yung Wage Order number 28 is separate from Wage Order 27.

3963
04:39:49,260 --> 04:39:50,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yun lang po, Madam Speaker, at least.

3964
04:39:51,080 --> 04:39:51,520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you.

3965
04:39:51,720 --> 04:39:55,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, this is of paramount importance.

3966
04:39:56,260 --> 04:40:02,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At ito po ang pagkakataon, Madam Speaker, na maliwanagan ang milyong-milyong mga manggagawa.

3967
04:40:02,500 --> 04:40:07,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So with the indulgence of our distinguished sponsor and Madam Speaker,

3968
04:40:08,180 --> 04:40:10,400
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: just a few more questions, Madam Speaker.

3969
04:40:10,820 --> 04:40:11,920
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Just one more question.

3970
04:40:12,160 --> 04:40:13,520
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Clarification on that matter.

3971
04:40:14,500 --> 04:40:20,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Binabanggit po ng Department of Labor and Employment na hindi isinusuko ang Wage Order 27,

3972
04:40:20,020 --> 04:40:21,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: but in effect,

3973
04:40:21,200 --> 04:40:22,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: sinusuko nila.

3974
04:40:22,800 --> 04:40:23,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Malinaw ang sinasabi.

3975
04:40:24,360 --> 04:40:26,720
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: If there is no bond, there is no injunction.

3976
04:40:27,140 --> 04:40:28,260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: That is the rules of court.

3977
04:40:29,380 --> 04:40:33,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Walang legal impediment, sabi ng Office of the Secretary General,

3978
04:40:33,880 --> 04:40:36,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: para ipatupad ang Wage Order 27.

3979
04:40:36,580 --> 04:40:44,740
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Binabanggit ng distinguished sponsor, ipatutupad ang Wage Order 28 bilang pamamaraan para ibigay sa mga manggagawa

3980
04:40:44,740 --> 04:40:49,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: yung 60 pesos mula doon sa first tranche.

3981
04:40:49,460 --> 04:40:51,080
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero hindi po yun ang punto.

3982
04:40:51,200 --> 04:40:57,380
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mula July 25, dahil walang hurisdiksyon ang Korte, kayo na po mismo ang nagsabi.

3983
04:40:57,800 --> 04:41:02,260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Dapat matanggap na ng bawat isang minimum wage earner yung 60 pesos.

3984
04:41:02,680 --> 04:41:07,540
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ibig sabihin, may kakulangan, may utang sa mga manggagawa na mahigit 3,000 piso.

3985
04:41:07,980 --> 04:41:10,860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ito po ang binabanggit natin, Mr. Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

3986
04:41:11,640 --> 04:41:16,360
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Hindi po maaaring isuplant ng Wage Order 28 yung Wage Order 27.

3987
04:41:16,360 --> 04:41:20,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So ang tanong dito, nilabag na nga ng DOLE.

3988
04:41:20,840 --> 04:41:24,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang sarili niyang guidelines na isang order lang ang ilalabas per year.

3989
04:41:25,780 --> 04:41:31,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tapos sinasabi niya na gumawa siya ng pamamaraan para maibigay yung unang tranche, 60 pesos.

3990
04:41:32,580 --> 04:41:37,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero kung susumahin natin, 60 pesos lang ang dagdag-saud sa Wage Order 28.

3991
04:41:38,360 --> 04:41:42,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ibig sabihin po ba, maglalabas ang DOLE ng panibagong Wage Order

3992
04:41:42,800 --> 04:41:47,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: para i-cover yung natitira mula doon sa Wage Order 27?

3993
04:41:47,840 --> 04:41:50,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mas pinapagulo ng DOLE.

3994
04:41:50,840 --> 04:41:54,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang kanyang buhay at ang kanyang sarili, pati ang mga manggagawa.

3995
04:41:55,360 --> 04:41:59,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Naiintindihan ko po ang binabanggit ng ating butihing sponsor, Madam Speaker.

3996
04:42:00,080 --> 04:42:01,640
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sasabihin nila na pamamaraan.

3997
04:42:02,000 --> 04:42:07,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero hindi po makuha ng mga manggagawa ang tindig ng Department of Labor and Employment

3998
04:42:07,100 --> 04:42:11,000
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na hindi nito bibitawan at isusuko ang Wage Order 27

3999
04:42:11,000 --> 04:42:16,260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at ipapatupad nito ang Wage Order 27 na malinaw na nakasulat sa batas.

4000
04:42:16,720 --> 04:42:20,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: DOLE na lang po ang hindi naniniwala na kaya niyang ipatupad.

4001
04:42:20,840 --> 04:42:22,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang Wage Order, Madam Speaker.

4002
04:42:23,060 --> 04:42:25,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, I will end here.

4003
04:42:26,620 --> 04:42:32,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang aming paniniwala po, kung hindi kayang tindigan ng Department of Labor and Employment

4004
04:42:32,180 --> 04:42:34,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang karapatan ng mga manggagawa,

4005
04:42:34,940 --> 04:42:39,420
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: it is in our firm position that the Department of Labor and Employment

4006
04:42:39,420 --> 04:42:43,320
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: should not ask this August Chamber for any budget

4007
04:42:43,320 --> 04:42:47,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: dahil pinakikita at pinatutunayan lang nito sa mga manggagawa

4008
04:42:47,040 --> 04:42:50,820
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na ang DOLE ay manhid, inutil at bingi.

4009
04:42:50,840 --> 04:42:53,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sa pakiramdam ng mga manggagawa.

4010
04:42:53,520 --> 04:42:56,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Intindihin nyo kung saan nang gagaling ang mga manggagawa.

4011
04:42:56,560 --> 04:42:58,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Para sa inyo, maliit na halaga lang ang 60 pesos.

4012
04:42:59,280 --> 04:43:01,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero sa bawat isang minimum wage earner na naririnig,

4013
04:43:03,000 --> 04:43:07,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang ating diskusyon ngayon, malaking bagay ang 3,000 pisong inagaw

4014
04:43:08,500 --> 04:43:11,000
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at pinagkait sa mga minimum wage earner.

4015
04:43:11,340 --> 04:43:14,520
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yun po ang pinatutungkulan ng representasyong ito.

4016
04:43:15,020 --> 04:43:16,700
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And at the appropriate time,

4017
04:43:16,700 --> 04:43:20,560
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: if the Department of Labor and Employment,

4018
04:43:20,840 --> 04:43:22,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: will not change its position

4019
04:43:22,800 --> 04:43:28,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at mananatili siya na matigas sa kanyang paninindigan

4020
04:43:28,680 --> 04:43:32,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na maglalabas ng bagong wage order sa halip na tindigan

4021
04:43:32,440 --> 04:43:33,720
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang lumang wage order,

4022
04:43:34,200 --> 04:43:37,060
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: this representation will make that motion

4023
04:43:37,060 --> 04:43:38,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at the appropriate time

4024
04:43:38,900 --> 04:43:43,580
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na ilagak na lang natin ang pondo ng Department of Labor and Employment

4025
04:43:43,580 --> 04:43:45,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: excluding TESDA.

4026
04:43:47,200 --> 04:43:50,380
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ilagak na lang yan sa ibang mga functions

4027
04:43:50,380 --> 04:43:51,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng ating gobyerno.

4028
04:43:52,360 --> 04:43:55,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Hindi po napatunayan ng Department of Labor and Employment

4029
04:43:55,440 --> 04:43:58,620
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na kaya niyang tindigan ang karapatan ng mga manggagawa.

4030
04:43:58,960 --> 04:44:02,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Sponsor, maraming salamat po sa inyong pagbigyan.

4031
04:44:02,200 --> 04:44:03,620
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

4032
04:44:03,940 --> 04:44:06,100
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pwede mo ba akong pagbigyan na sagutin yung huling statement mo?

4033
04:44:06,540 --> 04:44:08,660
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: For the record, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

4034
04:44:09,420 --> 04:44:12,180
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: alam po ninyo, kanina binanggit ko po

4035
04:44:12,180 --> 04:44:16,320
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na ang posisyon ng Departamento o DOLE

4036
04:44:16,320 --> 04:44:20,540
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay we impose na tinitindigan po namin

4037
04:44:20,540 --> 04:44:22,480
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ang wage order 27.

4038
04:44:22,840 --> 04:44:25,280
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Klaro po yun. It's on record na binanggit na po natin.

4039
04:44:25,760 --> 04:44:27,080
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And kahit tanongin mo po lahat dito,

4040
04:44:27,640 --> 04:44:29,080
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: yung po ay on record.

4041
04:44:29,760 --> 04:44:31,380
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kaya't hindi po namin pipwedeng tanggapin

4042
04:44:31,380 --> 04:44:35,660
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: with all due respect to my friend, Congressman Eli,

4043
04:44:36,300 --> 04:44:38,300
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sapagkat sabi ko nga rin kanina,

4044
04:44:38,980 --> 04:44:42,420
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kung kami talaga ay walang malasakit sa ating mga manggagawa,

4045
04:44:43,060 --> 04:44:45,100
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: alisana kami po ay hindi na po kumilos.

4046
04:44:45,600 --> 04:44:46,120
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Subalit,

4047
04:44:46,120 --> 04:44:48,980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sabi ko nga kanina sa pangungunan ng ating bagong sekretary,

4048
04:44:49,740 --> 04:44:52,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: we respect the legal proceedings.

4049
04:44:52,800 --> 04:44:53,400
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yan, alam mo yan.

4050
04:44:54,800 --> 04:44:55,460
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Alam mo yan.

4051
04:44:56,260 --> 04:44:56,960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Nakumbakit.

4052
04:44:57,880 --> 04:44:59,220
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero pinaninindigan po namin

4053
04:45:00,000 --> 04:45:05,940
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na ang Wage Order 27, we cannot prejudge kung ano sasabihin ng ating hudikotura.

4054
04:45:06,520 --> 04:45:07,500
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Nire-respeto namin yan.

4055
04:45:07,680 --> 04:45:10,620
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero ang sabi namin nga noon ng Dolly at Office ng OSG,

4056
04:45:11,120 --> 04:45:15,460
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay dapat ito ay implemented ng July 2025 o 2026,

4057
04:45:15,840 --> 04:45:18,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na dapat hindi nakikialam ang Korte.

4058
04:45:18,600 --> 04:45:20,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At yan naman po, alam mo rin po yan,

4059
04:45:20,680 --> 04:45:24,840
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na klaro sa Article 126 ng Labor Code na yun ang ating sinasabi.

4060
04:45:25,180 --> 04:45:27,060
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kaya sabi ko nga, Madam Speaker, for clarification,

4061
04:45:27,060 --> 04:45:31,720
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa lahat na nakikinig ng ating mga gawa na 1.1 million sa NCR.

4062
04:45:32,600 --> 04:45:39,340
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Una, yung 60 pesos po ng Wage 27 at 28 ay identical.

4063
04:45:40,320 --> 04:45:42,320
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pag sinabi mong nabawasan, hindi po.

4064
04:45:42,920 --> 04:45:46,380
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: I would like to quote you, my friend, Ellie, simple math.

4065
04:45:47,140 --> 04:45:50,940
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: 60 minus 60 is the same value.

4066
04:45:52,300 --> 04:45:54,560
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ngayon kung tatanungin mo, kanina,

4067
04:45:54,560 --> 04:45:57,060
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na kung magre-release na naman ng Wage,

4068
04:45:57,060 --> 04:46:00,420
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ang Wage Order para ito ay sa susunod na mga hakbang.

4069
04:46:00,800 --> 04:46:02,420
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And I know na alam mo po yan,

4070
04:46:02,740 --> 04:46:04,460
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: para klaro po sa ating nakikinig,

4071
04:46:04,820 --> 04:46:06,760
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kasi marami po yan at malaki po yan.

4072
04:46:07,340 --> 04:46:10,260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yung 60 pesos na po yun, pag minultiply mo sa 26 days,

4073
04:46:10,680 --> 04:46:12,340
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: that's 1,560.

4074
04:46:13,240 --> 04:46:15,680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yes, inaamin ng Dolly at ng Wage Board

4075
04:46:15,680 --> 04:46:21,160
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na hindi lahat ng problema ay masusulusyonan doon sa 1,560.

4076
04:46:21,720 --> 04:46:22,860
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero malaking bagay ito.

4077
04:46:23,140 --> 04:46:25,420
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: At ito po, uulitin ko po, for the record,

4078
04:46:25,420 --> 04:46:26,860
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay tinitindigan.

4079
04:46:27,060 --> 04:46:30,520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Nang Departamento kasama ang OSG.

4080
04:46:31,260 --> 04:46:37,040
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sabi ko nga po, once that document from the Judiciary,

4081
04:46:37,780 --> 04:46:40,820
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: binanggit na lang ating mahal na Secretary Francis Torrentino,

4082
04:46:41,240 --> 04:46:43,780
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ipapatupad po natin ang mga Wage Orders

4083
04:46:43,780 --> 04:46:47,020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na ating pinanilindigan para sa ating mga manggagawa

4084
04:46:47,020 --> 04:46:50,680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa NCR o sa buong Pilipinas sa mga darating na panahon.

4085
04:46:51,080 --> 04:46:52,600
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sana ay kahit pa paano,

4086
04:46:52,600 --> 04:46:56,220
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: nasagot namin yung itanong Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

4087
04:46:57,060 --> 04:46:59,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat, Distinguished Sponsor.

4088
04:46:59,280 --> 04:47:03,320
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Thank you very much, Congressman Eli San Fernando.

4089
04:47:03,460 --> 04:47:04,160
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader?

4090
04:47:05,380 --> 04:47:07,260
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize

4091
04:47:07,260 --> 04:47:10,520
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: the Honorable Antonio Tinio of the ACT Teachers Party-list

4092
04:47:10,520 --> 04:47:12,620
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to interpolate on the proposed budget.

4093
04:47:13,300 --> 04:47:15,960
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Tinio is hereby recognized for his interpellation.

4094
04:47:17,720 --> 04:47:19,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker,

4095
04:47:20,820 --> 04:47:24,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa Distinguished Sponsor at sa Department of Labor and Employment.

4096
04:47:24,220 --> 04:47:25,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilang mga katanungan po.

4097
04:47:26,400 --> 04:47:27,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, of course,

4098
04:47:27,060 --> 04:47:31,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: una, dahil ahensya po ito ng Department of Labor and Employment,

4099
04:47:31,360 --> 04:47:35,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: of course, ang tanong natin ay kaugnay sa sahod.

4100
04:47:37,160 --> 04:47:42,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At dapat meron po tayong graphic dyan.

4101
04:47:44,480 --> 04:47:45,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ayan, of course.

4102
04:47:46,640 --> 04:47:48,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course, usapin ng minimum wage.

4103
04:47:48,800 --> 04:47:52,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At alam natin, ang umiiral na patakaran at batas at patakaran ngayon,

4104
04:47:52,980 --> 04:47:55,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: regional, ang setting ng minimum wage.

4105
04:47:55,980 --> 04:47:59,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, dito, sinasummarize, galing sa IBO nito,

4106
04:48:00,060 --> 04:48:06,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sinasummarize yung mga regional wage levels per region.

4107
04:48:08,680 --> 04:48:14,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course, ang pinakamataas dyan ay sa NCR.

4108
04:48:18,280 --> 04:48:20,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, hindi nga updated yan.

4109
04:48:20,420 --> 04:48:22,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That particular graphic,

4110
04:48:23,360 --> 04:48:25,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang mga rates ngayon,

4111
04:48:25,980 --> 04:48:27,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: alam naman natin, for NCR,

4112
04:48:28,400 --> 04:48:29,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: it's already 755.

4113
04:48:31,720 --> 04:48:31,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

4114
04:48:37,940 --> 04:48:39,820
